{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion (RNA + image) provides any signal over simpler baselines. config_009 is the simplest multimodal setup: singleprofile, PCA (n=2000) for RNA, ResNet50 for image, and a basic concat fusion with no aggregation. This directly tests the core hypothesis of the study—does combining modalities help—while using well-established, low-complexity components. Expected relative cost is LOW-MODERATE (PCA is trivial, ResNet50 is standard, no transformer or large ViT, single profile), preserving GPU budget for the remaining 9 experiments. If it performs well, I can escalate to multiprofile, scgpt/scvi encoders, or transformer aggregation in subsequent runs; if it underperforms, it isolates whether the issue is the fusion strategy or the modalities themselves, guiding targeted exploration. Starting with the simplest informative configuration minimizes confounds and maximizes the information gained per GPU hour in this first experiment."
}

